      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note on cumulative comment size limit: `Documentation/config-gerrit.txt` promises that base64 images are not counted against either `change.commentSizeLimit` or `change.cumulativeCommentSizeLimit`. However, `CreateDraftComment`, `PutDraftComment`, and `PostReviewOp` only strip images from the transient `CommentForValidation` objects while persisting the full raw `comment.message` in NoteDb.\n\nWhen any subsequent comment is posted on the same change, `CommentCumulativeSizeValidator.validateComments` sums `Comment::getApproximateSize` across all existing `notes.getHumanComments()` (which uses the unstripped `comment.message.length()`). As a result, a single ~3 MiB screenshot comment silently exhausts the default 3 MiB `change.cumulativeCommentSizeLimit` and blocks all subsequent comments on the CL (`Exceeding maximum cumulative size of comments and change messages`).\n\nConsider injecting `MarkdownImagesUtil` into `CommentCumulativeSizeValidator` (in this CL or a follow-up) so existing persisted comment sizes also exclude base64 images when `change.allowMarkdownBase64ImagesInComments` is enabled.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "af5000d8e3e86e41fe3e1aefaeda54b9f74978dd",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
