      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T20:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `PostReviewOp.validateComments`, the size passed to `CommentForValidation.create` is computed as:\n\n```java\nint size \u003d\n    comment.getApproximateSize()\n        - comment.message.length()\n        + strippedMessage.length();\n```\n\nwhich preserves the approximate size of non-message fields (`fixSuggestions`, metadata fields). Passing `strippedMessage.length()` directly here means a draft with `fixSuggestions` or long metadata near `change.commentSizeLimit` can pass draft validation and then fail at publish time in `PostReviewOp`.\n\nSuggested update:\n\n```java\n    String strippedMessage \u003d markdownImagesUtil.stripImages(comment.message);\n    int size \u003d\n        comment.getApproximateSize() - comment.message.length() + strippedMessage.length();\n    ImmutableList\u003cCommentValidationFailure\u003e validationFailures \u003d\n        PublishCommentUtil.findInvalidComments(\n            ctx,\n            commentValidators,\n            ImmutableList.of(\n                CommentForValidation.create(\n                    CommentSource.HUMAN,\n                    comment.lineNbr \u003e 0 ? CommentType.INLINE_COMMENT : CommentType.FILE_COMMENT,\n                    strippedMessage,\n                    size)));\n```",
